#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119580 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "38fce106-2ba8-554c-ace3-a5731d15a635" :question/math-academy-id "e-4949" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/assets/40ec5f2b2615eedf6b16420a2089b7c377141db46237de35218c5e685b629918.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/assets/0589ebbdb2c14b93e1296b9e1f8b0caa0c3df49bff4c9fbb97e4c18102844ec1.png)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119581 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/id #uuid "74693316-2e5a-5821-87a5-fdc5b8719c82" :question/math-academy-id "e-4950" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1538dde4-ab62-502e-8efe-7f37628ab861" :question/math-academy-id "e-4951" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2dfb090-8668-52ad-87bd-7b0c2cb7dc62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388031} {:answer/id #uuid "ce7dfdef-a6f6-53cf-91a1-51499188e0a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388032} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca79318-c292-567b-b18d-294f042b379e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388033} {:answer/id #uuid "c423bea4-eabc-5c5c-8335-12e04762c48a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388034} {:answer/id #uuid "9e3905ae-e406-5602-8a76-21672e1b8986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ca79318-c292-567b-b18d-294f042b379e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388033} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cbf1f02-a404-5378-a26b-f2713a97b4a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ad8882e-4e17-5620-b084-21aafa42032d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129094" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(1,2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(1,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0\\cdot (-2)+(-4)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e2ca9a1-fb24-5712-925c-5959e12d4c2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388038} {:answer/id #uuid "4019b38c-aa2b-5ec7-a820-42d26bea3bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388039} {:answer/id #uuid "802b8e11-2584-5155-a4cd-2ebfe252af39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388040} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7c4579-cee8-5fb1-815b-20318945d169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388041} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c6e63e-b389-5e51-b321-fb6bce740b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f7c4579-cee8-5fb1-815b-20318945d169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388041} :answer-field/id #uuid "e836f468-f33f-5437-852e-2bfa512d2628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57b9ef22-fb1b-538b-ae87-f09c0b621f1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129098" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,3,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨6,-1,5⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-2⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,-1,5).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,-1,5⟩-⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,-4,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-8-12|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{3} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0809196-b366-5886-afff-771bfdd37057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339544} {:answer/id #uuid "01d9145c-b484-579b-918d-29cc61be229c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339545} {:answer/id #uuid "930bf38c-95a5-5e07-b7a1-cab2e79b5552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339546} {:answer/id #uuid "5a6e7e2e-8e2d-56fa-9404-e7e906b75117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339547} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8a1f4b-0370-5f4f-9f89-4c4efeaff742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a6e7e2e-8e2d-56fa-9404-e7e906b75117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339547} :answer-field/id #uuid "5158d59b-b675-5738-8559-519928423666" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9353c0c9-bae4-5a82-8f86-8a66dcc33c88" :question/math-academy-id "q-129100" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d34557c-9668-573a-b832-0e087b548a78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388045} {:answer/id #uuid "c8508785-7cce-5b15-a748-06f59d173d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388046} {:answer/id #uuid "197ef296-f4e1-510f-a17f-7a953b342003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388047} {:answer/id #uuid "2875b1e3-3614-576a-98fe-8d853f1d9a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388048} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7982c3-8b00-5fc8-86c3-9aa66b34bb45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "197ef296-f4e1-510f-a17f-7a953b342003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388047} :answer-field/id #uuid "575c10d3-5e8b-5ded-aacf-435058c1f6a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b78702ba-d6e3-50bb-96e7-281310599418" :question/math-academy-id "q-129119" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-3,7)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨6,3,-2⟩=-17$, find the shortest distance from $P(2,-6,2)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-3,7⟩-⟨2,-6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,3,-2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 6+3\\cdot 3+5\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+9-10|}{\\sqrt{36+9+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a9c101-6040-5f1b-801d-2fbfe20bc200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383253} {:answer/id #uuid "63bf3027-e5e3-5155-a2ae-b3868a2b239d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383254} {:answer/id #uuid "c18299b4-08b7-5050-bdf0-67673df597ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383255} {:answer/id #uuid "44c339db-5776-5817-80dc-407ee9a16d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383256} {:answer/id #uuid "ab946482-d5f1-5b8b-afec-fe7af533a64c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63bf3027-e5e3-5155-a2ae-b3868a2b239d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383254} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a8dd7df-6ab1-5986-87a4-4cf5c94f9847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "780bb8b5-f350-5f18-b702-f18d3b60c284" :question/math-academy-id "q-129120" :question/problem "Given that $Q(5,-1,9)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,-2⟩=3$, find the shortest distance from $P(7,-2,8)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,9⟩-⟨7,-2,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨3,-6,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-2)\\cdot 3+1\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6-6-2|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-14|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8eaacf8-bb02-5974-8bbc-0c424a836d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388052} {:answer/id #uuid "bebba3c6-ca59-5e2e-8a7c-51a59b84e7e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{30}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388053} {:answer/id #uuid "87aadc4b-2eef-5b06-9aa0-aef0ec8b3955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388054} {:answer/id #uuid "09f05e42-531e-50ab-8024-b477c36efdc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388055} {:answer/id #uuid "05569caf-db27-5128-987f-36082784f425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87aadc4b-2eef-5b06-9aa0-aef0ec8b3955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388054} :answer-field/id #uuid "975ae3ec-ee75-592b-af2a-76eb70da9777" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3db73ba-3f2a-5efa-9740-ea27b4704163" :question/math-academy-id "q-129158" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,3,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x+2y+3z=9.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=0$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+2y+3z & =9 \\\\ 6(1)+2(0)+3z & =9 \\\\ 3z & =3 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,0,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 6+(-3)\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12-6+15|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8db587ce-69aa-581a-be6a-29d92bf6b14e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352135} {:answer/id #uuid "42e846d8-f031-5281-a2b2-dc7db84e8aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352136} {:answer/id #uuid "48209447-a767-5708-b0d0-1ff8956e3296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352137} {:answer/id #uuid "d867d796-7544-56a4-84f1-87fc57408402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352138} {:answer/id #uuid "aafb01de-a3ee-585a-be34-e44b278c8b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48209447-a767-5708-b0d0-1ff8956e3296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352137} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b8abed5-7b3e-5cbc-89ed-00237df2fd1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b6ae898-0635-54c5-a55e-aacad2ce72c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-129163" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1df2aa2-eb37-5616-97f6-4481d549c40d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388059} {:answer/id #uuid "e3353ea6-2843-5a76-b5d4-764fe8c24aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388060} {:answer/id #uuid "9260b66a-78b7-50ba-b4cf-126db8f8f862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388061} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a21add-654c-59af-a497-2c78f4bae05c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388062} {:answer/id #uuid "b0436aca-68e1-58a6-b776-41a3792590b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0436aca-68e1-58a6-b776-41a3792590b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388063} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0df5def-2690-59ba-8217-e030c44d7922" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64474450-57b0-5c05-b9ab-5a9f07006716" :question/math-academy-id "q-129165" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,4,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x+2y+z=6.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y+z & =6 \\\\ -2(1)+2(1)+z & =6 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,6)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,6⟩-⟨-1,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,2,1⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2+11\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4-6+11|}{\\sqrt{4+4+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f57623c-c55f-52b0-913f-67767ee78be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388066} {:answer/id #uuid "3540da61-087b-5611-9bb8-d617f70adcf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388067} {:answer/id #uuid "3b17e62d-3a9d-5f3b-9586-0711e6fe25ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388068} {:answer/id #uuid "ece26e44-69e8-5a2f-ad9a-379b10b8b18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388069} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc77481-07aa-5231-a289-93d360d16b65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3540da61-087b-5611-9bb8-d617f70adcf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388067} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec0dd06-964d-57df-b4ad-6f1af1a827b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e76cfdfc-9b56-58a0-97cf-11779b75f58e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33451" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(2,0,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,3,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4+6+18|}{\\sqrt{1+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|28|}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51676e50-b7f0-5eed-97fd-1d3a493444f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352142} {:answer/id #uuid "7417c09d-0a95-532b-8866-0a6e02280014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352143} {:answer/id #uuid "28f5b5fa-ac8e-5c0c-a526-a48566199827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352144} {:answer/id #uuid "487132b9-07c4-5126-93d7-c72103039bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352145} {:answer/id #uuid "a03e5b55-0198-5d77-b267-35bc98a33873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28f5b5fa-ac8e-5c0c-a526-a48566199827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352144} :answer-field/id #uuid "bea90a28-9d85-5ebf-9862-ad129369fe84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "088dd097-0f42-5df8-97da-74581538794b" :question/math-academy-id "q-33454" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,-2,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩=27.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩ & =27 \\\\ -3x+2y+3z & =27 \\\\ 3z & =27+3x-2y \\\\ z & =9+x-\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=6$ and $y=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+6-\\frac{2}{3}(3)=13.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(6,3,13)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,3,13⟩-⟨4,-2,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,5,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,2,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+10+18|}{\\sqrt{9+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|22|}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc2dba1e-8f98-58fe-823e-1230282e48a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388073} {:answer/id #uuid "b18e5a68-4f92-52a3-93d5-b1ba3ff1b96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388074} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e6097c-f2aa-50f4-9197-bcdaa731e9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388075} {:answer/id #uuid "9547d3a4-9003-5f74-81ab-fbd584a90edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388076} {:answer/id #uuid "30026039-efa5-5cdc-ba38-3a38b0e526e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b18e5a68-4f92-52a3-93d5-b1ba3ff1b96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388074} :answer-field/id #uuid "90d74317-b6b9-59b7-9f6b-a6807df4ac4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "798f9001-1171-56bf-9055-27ac210d1a3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-33467" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,15,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,9,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-5)+(-6)\\cdot 1+7\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-6-14|}{\\sqrt{25+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5dbb4f7-a168-5c56-ba5f-427586a8ca88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339586} {:answer/id #uuid "aef8c0f8-5bff-53ed-94eb-9f3509d2c564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339587} {:answer/id #uuid "d860b881-ac6e-5c4f-8deb-ef47d7352a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\sqrt{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339588} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe74019-90c7-56ae-a6db-b9792c8659db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339589} {:answer/id #uuid "0ad6d0cf-316c-53f5-83dd-40500e598bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ad6d0cf-316c-53f5-83dd-40500e598bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339590} :answer-field/id #uuid "b28316c9-bd52-50a8-9c35-e588b75348a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8c5c6cc-9743-5139-a5ed-91098db233ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-80049" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Simplified Dot Product Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077d3150-975a-51a9-9216-1a486213b1d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383267} {:answer/id #uuid "daf22698-4613-5982-8786-c0d5ba6cad6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383268} {:answer/id #uuid "c801d42b-7f0d-5c60-b475-a966bee05aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383269} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c364af-a272-50a6-b30f-494f110bb9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383270} {:answer/id #uuid "243ec44e-50c3-5f68-80bc-c86f4f16c78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c364af-a272-50a6-b30f-494f110bb9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383270} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab6f04e5-e374-58d3-a929-8a7e744125e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7b651ee-2f62-5743-a764-86bdae6d7be2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80115" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,11,1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩=20.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩ & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,9⟩-⟨-2,11,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-7,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨2,-5,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e558ecab-5f69-5424-95ee-e1dd4980e47a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388080} {:answer/id #uuid "9c927585-21bd-5aa6-83d1-eba5edef5c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388081} {:answer/id #uuid "7e08333a-8917-5b00-8b22-cb9bc9295244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388082} {:answer/id #uuid "0f556574-f92e-55ca-8bea-9054417e807a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388083} {:answer/id #uuid "4370c4e8-8840-520c-96e0-4331576b55a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e08333a-8917-5b00-8b22-cb9bc9295244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388082} :answer-field/id #uuid "755bb3bd-a2cf-5132-b8cd-fdefe65fb60f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0ef2c7b-5cf6-5fcb-8997-f9ad34a75174" :question/math-academy-id "q-80118" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,5,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-8y+8z=-36.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+8z & =-36 \\\\ 4(-1)-8(1)+8z & =-36 \\\\ 8z & =-24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,1,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,1,-3⟩-⟨-7,5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-4,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-8,8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-8)+(-5)\\cdot 8|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+32-40|}{\\sqrt{16+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,16\\,|}{\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Shortest Distance Between a Point and a Plane Given in Cartesian Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "738fe9d0-29e4-585e-96c3-a87a2ba470c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388087} {:answer/id #uuid "3a2d4d69-26e7-530d-a76b-d30a13e39d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388088} {:answer/id #uuid "9360ea04-76db-54eb-b194-f517cb548b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388089} {:answer/id #uuid "07bbc60f-8158-5f0a-a653-c579ea16a240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388090} {:answer/id #uuid "c546b4e3-152d-5562-8845-17b2fd19d627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9360ea04-76db-54eb-b194-f517cb548b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388089} :answer-field/id #uuid "57b99d77-9bee-5bb6-97d4-878cc0b372d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9001a16-7619-5368-a4e0-2e300550bbbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-80123" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,-1,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-4x-2y+2z=16.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-2y+2z & =16 \\\\ -4(-1)-2(2)+2z & =16 \\\\ 2z & =16 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,2,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,2,8⟩-⟨-4,-1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-4,-2,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6+6|}{\\sqrt{16+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
